%erg 0.1
Title: migrate: also rewrite hook erg_bin path
Created: 2026-05-20
Author: MinhHaDuong

--- log ---
2026-05-20T09:51Z MinhHaDuong created

--- body ---

## Context

When migrating from the legacy layout (binary at `tickets/tools/go/erg`,
plus `tickets/tools/go/main.go` source) to the new bootstrap layout
(binary at `tickets/erg`, no in-repo Go sources), `erg migrate`
correctly:

- Rewrites ticket files (`%erg v1` → `%erg 0.1`, drops `Status:`, etc.)
- Moves the binary to the new path
- Updates `tickets/AGENTS.md` and `tickets/spec-erg-v1.md`

But it does NOT rewrite `.git/hooks/pre-commit`, which still contains:

```sh
erg_bin="tickets/tools/go/erg"
...
if ! "$erg_bin" validate tickets/; then
```

Two things are stale:

1. **Binary path**: `tickets/tools/go/erg` no longer exists; the new
   bootstrap binary lives at `tickets/erg`. The hook fails with
   `ERROR: erg binary not found. Run 'make build' first.` — but there
   is no Makefile any more either.
2. **CLI surface**: the hook calls `erg validate tickets/` (directory
   form), which the new binary rejects with
   `ERROR: tickets/ is a directory; use 'erg check tickets/' for
   directory validation`. Corpus checks are now `erg check [DIR]`.

Observed today (2026-05-20) on padme after migrating: the user could
not commit any ticket-bearing change without manually patching the
hook between the `# --- git-erg ---` markers.

## Actions

1. In `erg migrate`, detect a managed pre-commit hook (presence of
   `# --- git-erg --- begin/end` markers) and rewrite the fragment in
   place:
   - `erg_bin="tickets/tools/go/erg"` → `erg_bin="tickets/erg"`
   - `"$erg_bin" validate tickets/` → `"$erg_bin" check tickets/`
2. If the hook fragment is missing (user removed it) or unmanaged
   (markers absent), don't touch the hook; print a clear notice
   suggesting `erg init` or a manual update.
3. Add a regression test: a fixture repo with the legacy hook, run
   `erg migrate`, assert the hook now references the new paths and
   passes a sample commit.
4. Document the hook auto-update in the migration changelog so users
   know to re-stage the hook if they had local edits.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `erg migrate` rewrites managed pre-commit hooks to the new
      binary path and corpus-check CLI form.
- [ ] Regression test covers the rewrite.
- [ ] A user who upgrades from the legacy layout can `git commit
      tickets/...` without touching `.git/hooks/pre-commit`.
